      "artist": "G41rn8",
      "description": "Thousand-Buddha Hall. Lingyan Si, Jinan\nThe foundation of this hall dates originally to the Tang dynasty, but the building itself was reconstructed in the Song, Ming, Qing, and modern eras. It contains the most important statues in the temple: a Vairocana triad, and 40 Arhats. The Pizhi Pagoda is peeking up behind the roof.",
